        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "body",
          "value": {
            "markup": "<p>Model-Context Protocol (MCP) represents a fundamental shift in how content management systems interact with external tools and services. Unlike traditional APIs that require custom integration code, MCP provides a standardized interface that enables seamless communication between Umbraco and a wide variety of applications.</p><p><strong>Key advantages of MCP:</strong></p><ul><li>Standardized protocol for content management automation</li><li>Seamless integration with multiple tools through a single interface</li><li>Reduced development time for custom integrations</li><li>Future-proof architecture that evolves with the ecosystem</li><li>Enhanced security through role-based access control</li></ul><p>MCP is transforming how teams manage content at scale, enabling real-time synchronization between Umbraco and external services without the overhead of custom middleware.</p>",
            "blocks": {
              "layout": {},
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": []
            }
          }
